% Rx_Cass_NS.in -- NS twin of Rx_Cass_FarField.in: the Primary is
% Element= NSReflector (single-member non-sequential group; geometry
% identical to the sequential twin Rx_Cass_NSseq.in, which differs in
% that one token only).  Fixture for the dw_dsurf NSReflector
% eligibility gate (tDwDsurf).
% Obscratn= 2.4 (annular launch, r_in 1.2): with a full disk, every
% ray inside r ~ 1.005 takes a wrong turn through the NS dispatch on
% this deep-conic train and dies (surface miss at elt 4) while the
% annulus is piston-exact vs sequential -- suspected ConSrf
% root-by-proximity via the NS block; engine follow-on filed in
% macos/BRIEF_luis_round3.md.  Repro: set Obscratn= 0 here.
% Chief-ray note: the chief launches at r = 0 (inside the NS wrong-turn
% zone) and goes geometrically dead on the NS twin (the deck's one
% expected surface miss; obscured-class anyway, OPD unaffected).  Do
% NOT use FEX / reset_xp machinery on Rx_Cass_NS.in until the engine
% follow-on resolves -- single-field gates only.

